<article class="env-remark" id="03TR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03TR">Remark <span data-tag="03TR">59.77.4</span>.</a> Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. Let $X$ be a scheme. For a bounded complex $K^\bullet $ of constructible flat $\Lambda $-modules on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ each stalk $K^ p_{\overline{x}}$ is a finite projective $\Lambda $-module. Hence the stalks of the complex are perfect complexes of $\Lambda $-modules. </p>
